cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Supply-network disruption surrogate: counterfactual impact, not a risk score"
abstract: >-
  A learned temporal graph surrogate for a mechanistic multi-echelon supply-network
  simulator. Instead of scoring suppliers on their own features, the model answers a
  counterfactual - if this node or lane fails, what happens to service level at each
  demand point, when, and for how long - and is validated against the simulator as an
  exact oracle. Includes the reference-style tabular baseline, a parameter-matched
  no-message-passing ablation, calibrated predictive intervals, generalisation tests
  along four named distribution-shift axes, and a decision-quality-at-fixed-compute
  comparison against running the simulator directly.
type: software
